WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.598
"I'm going to miss you, Brenda," Leah said on the last day of school.

2
00:00:07.599 --> 00:00:13.557
"I'll call you when I get back from New York," Brenda promised.

3
00:00:13.558 --> 00:00:18.653
"Where is your family going for summer vacation, Leah?" asked Kylie.

4
00:00:18.654 --> 00:00:25.356
"I don't know yet," Leah admitted. "But I hope it's somewhere awesome."

5
00:00:25.357 --> 00:00:30.343
That evening Leah asked her mother about their family's vacation plans.

6
00:00:30.344 --> 00:00:35.533
"Actually your dad and I were going to discuss that with you and Paul tonight," Mom said.

7
00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:39.860
"Is it a surprise?" Leah asked excitedly.

8
00:00:39.861 --> 00:00:46.484
"Yes," Mom answered mysteriously. "It's somewhere both new and familiar."

9
00:00:46.485 --> 00:00:52.171
"Hmm," Leah thought curiously. "Where could it be?"

10
00:00:52.172 --> 00:00:56.583
Leah was definitely looking forward to her family's trip this year.

11
00:00:56.584 --> 00:01:02.076
A year earlier an unexpected hardship had occurred.

12
00:01:02.077 --> 00:01:08.725
"My company decided to lay off workers," Leah's dad had told them one night at dinner.

13
00:01:08.726 --> 00:01:13.033
"What does 'lay off' mean?" Leah asked.

14
00:01:13.034 --> 00:01:18.605
"It means they are cutting jobs, including mine," he informed her sadly.

15
00:01:18.606 --> 00:01:23.071
"I'll find another job, but it might take some time."

16
00:01:23.072 --> 00:01:27.140
Months had passed before Dad found another job.

17
00:01:27.141 --> 00:01:33.680
He was relieved to be working again, but his new salary was much lower than his old salary.

18
00:01:33.681 --> 00:01:39.019
That meant everyone in the family still had to make sacrifices.

19
00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:42.528
Leah had to give up taking art classes.

20
00:01:42.529 --> 00:01:48.175
"When our finances improve, you can resume your art lessons," Dad promised.

21
00:01:48.176 --> 00:01:51.639
That night the family sat down together.

22
00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:56.775
"We've been considering where to go this year," Dad began.

23
00:01:56.776 --> 00:02:02.333
"We want to go somewhere to relax and enjoy time together as a family," added Mom.

24
00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:06.145
"And finally we thought of the best place to do that."

25
00:02:06.146 --> 00:02:09.525
"Where is it?" Leah blurted out.

26
00:02:09.526 --> 00:02:15.296
Her parents exchanged glances. "At home!" they said in unison.

27
00:02:15.297 --> 00:02:20.670
Paul and Leah were stunned. "Are you kidding?" Paul asked.

28
00:02:20.671 --> 00:02:26.583
Mom and Dad shook their heads. "We're perfectly serious," said Mom.

29
00:02:26.584 --> 00:02:33.058
"We're not going to Disneyland? Or Vancouver?" Leah asked in dismay.

30
00:02:33.059 --> 00:02:39.151
"You don't have to travel to an exotic destination to enjoy a vacation," Mom said cheerfully.

31
00:02:39.152 --> 00:02:48.518
"But all my friends are traveling somewhere!" Leah choked back her tears. "Brenda is going to New York!"

32
00:02:48.519 --> 00:02:51.898
Her parents seemed unconcerned.

33
00:02:51.899 --> 00:02:57.322
"Our vacation is for three days." Dad opened a notebook.

34
00:02:57.323 --> 00:03:01.044
"And during our vacation, there are some essential rules.

35
00:03:01.045 --> 00:03:05.689
Rule number one: No television, Internet, or telephone."

36
00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:09.059
"What?" shouted Paul.

37
00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:14.522
"Rule number two," Dad said. "Each of us takes a turn preparing a meal."

38
00:03:14.523 --> 00:03:19.405
"But that's Mom's job," Leah protested.

39
00:03:19.406 --> 00:03:23.673
"I want a vacation too," Mom stated.

40
00:03:23.674 --> 00:03:30.788
"And rule number three: We spend most of our time together. We are not to isolate ourselves."

41
00:03:30.789 --> 00:03:38.885
"Ugh." Leah groaned. This was going to be the strangest— and worst—family vacation ever.

42
00:03:38.886 --> 00:03:43.654
On the first day of vacation, Leah and Paul were in the family room.

43
00:03:43.655 --> 00:03:46.419
Leah had found some books to read.

44
00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:52.681
Paul was looking for something. "Where's the remote?" he called.

45
00:03:52.682 --> 00:03:57.093
"Rule number one, Paul," Dad reminded him.

46
00:03:57.094 --> 00:04:03.062
"No television." He held up a box. "How about working on this with me?"

47
00:04:03.063 --> 00:04:05.782
"What is it?" asked Paul.

48
00:04:05.783 --> 00:04:08.866
"A model airplane," said Dad.

49
00:04:08.867 --> 00:04:12.106
Paul shrugged. "Sure."

50
00:04:12.107 --> 00:04:16.621
Mom sat down next to Leah. "Can I keep you company?"

51
00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:24.738
"Okay." Leah looked up from her book as her mother started working on something at the table. "What's that, Mom?"

52
00:04:24.739 --> 00:04:28.455
"A jigsaw puzzle. And I could definitely use your help."

53
00:04:28.456 --> 00:04:33.789
Mom moved over to make room for Leah, and the two of them worked on the puzzle for a while.

54
00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:37.194
That night Dad prepared dinner.

55
00:04:37.195 --> 00:04:42.871
"I hope he doesn't burn the kitchen down!" whispered Mom to Leah and Paul.

56
00:04:42.872 --> 00:04:49.827
"I hope whatever he makes is edible!" Leah said with a giggle.

57
00:04:49.828 --> 00:04:55.117
"Hey! No insulting the chef!" Dad shouted from the kitchen.

58
00:04:55.118 --> 00:04:58.368
Everyone sat down and looked at the food.

59
00:04:58.369 --> 00:05:03.038
"Just try it. You're going to love it!" Dad said.

60
00:05:03.039 --> 00:05:11.611
Leah wasn't sure what it was, but she sampled the meal anyway. "Actually this is pretty good, Dad."

61
00:05:11.612 --> 00:05:15.621
After dinner the family looked at some old photos.

62
00:05:15.622 --> 00:05:20.593
Soon everyone was trading memories about when Leah and Paul were younger.

63
00:05:20.594 --> 00:05:26.597
"Oh, I remember this picture," said Mom. "That was Paul's first bicycle."

64
00:05:26.598 --> 00:05:33.117
"Hey, I remember that bike. What happened to it?" Paul asked.

65
00:05:33.118 --> 00:05:37.603
The next morning Leah saw that Paul was up early.

66
00:05:37.604 --> 00:05:41.191
"I'm reporting for chef duty," Paul said.

67
00:05:41.192 --> 00:05:45.207
"What are you making for breakfast, Paul?" Mom wanted to know.

68
00:05:45.208 --> 00:05:50.834
"The only thing I know how to make," said Paul.

69
00:05:50.835 --> 00:05:59.903
"Hot dogs? For breakfast?" Leah burst out. "That sounds absolutely delicious!"

70
00:05:59.904 --> 00:06:04.905
Later that day Leah and Paul listened to some music together.

71
00:06:04.906 --> 00:06:08.950
And before bedtime, the family played a board game together.

72
00:06:08.951 --> 00:06:12.583
It was Leah and Dad versus Paul and Mom.

73
00:06:12.584 --> 00:06:16.271
Soon Leah landed on the history category.

74
00:06:16.272 --> 00:06:26.538
"Name the young Macedonian leader who conquered Persia at the age of 25," Paul read aloud. "You can't help her, Dad!"

75
00:06:26.539 --> 00:06:32.532
"I got it!" Leah called triumphantly. "Alexander the Great!"

76
00:06:32.533 --> 00:06:37.921
"Wow, how did you get to be so intelligent?" Dad asked.

77
00:06:37.922 --> 00:06:42.923
On the last day of the vacation, everyone did whatever he or she wanted.

78
00:06:42.924 --> 00:06:46.482
Leah read a book. Mom painted her toenails.

79
00:06:46.483 --> 00:06:50.755
Dad and Paul worked on the airplane model together.

80
00:06:50.756 --> 00:06:56.124
"Ta-da!" They proudly displayed the airplane when it was finally finished.

81
00:06:56.125 --> 00:07:00.759
"It looks fantastic," said Leah.

82
00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:05.349
"Dad and I make a good team," Paul said proudly.

83
00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:11.864
"This was one of the most relaxing vacations I ever had," Dad announced later on.

84
00:07:11.865 --> 00:07:18.438
"I agree." Mom nodded. "I got to spend a lot of quality time with my children and my husband."

85
00:07:18.439 --> 00:07:23.782
"I got to build a model airplane!" Paul said, grinning at Dad.

86
00:07:23.783 --> 00:07:28.228
Leah sat, quietly contemplating the vacation for a minute.

87
00:07:28.229 --> 00:07:32.922
Last week she had not been looking forward to her family's vacation at all.

88
00:07:32.923 --> 00:07:42.567
While her friends were traveling to faraway destinations, she'd be stuck here, with only boring stuff to do. But she had realized something.

89
00:07:42.568 --> 00:07:46.041
Leah smiled at Mom, Dad, and Paul.

90
00:07:46.042 --> 00:08:02.386
"Spending time with your family—even when you stay at home—is the best vacation ever!"

